ate respiratory care for a resident when needed.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0711":{"code":"F-0711","title":"Ensure the resident's doctor reviews the resident's care, writes, signs and dates progress notes and orders, at each required visit.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0755":{"code":"F-0755","title":"Provide pharmaceutical services to meet the needs of each resident and employ or obtain the services of a licensed pharmacist.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0924":{"code":"F-0924","title":"Put firmly secured handrails on each side of hallways.","category":"Environmental Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0585":{"code":"F-0585","title":"Honor the resident's right to voice grievances without discrimination or reprisal and the facility must establish a grievance policy and make prompt efforts to resolve grievances.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0600":{"code":"F-0600","title":"Protect each resident from all types of abuse such as physical, mental, sexual abuse, physical punishment, and neglect by anybody.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-